.TH DANBY-SKIJUMP 1
.SH NAME
danby-skijump \- takeoff and aerodynamic flight of a ski jumper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/skijump
.SH MODEL
The jumper leaves the ramp at a selected speed and angle.  Relative airspeed,
including headwind, determines quadratic drag and aerodynamic lift; gravity
completes the flight equations.
.SH DISPLAY
The spatial plot shows height versus distance and telemetry shows speed.
Tracks alter takeoff speed, ramp angle, drag, lift, headwind, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/skijump.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
